==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|catatony||dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.|catatonia}}, from {{der|en|grc|κατάτονος|t=more broad than high}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A severe [[psychiatric]] condition, often associated with [[schizophrenia]], characterized by a [[tendency]] to remain in a [[rigid]] state of [[stupor]] for long [[period]]s which give way to short periods of extreme [[agitation]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} A frozen, unresponsive state, as of electronic equipment.
#* '''1998''', David Drake, Thomas T. Thomas, ''Crisis of Empire Book I: An Honorable Defense''
#*: “Relay that!” Thwaite shouted. Somewhere on the bridge a hand closed over a relay and dropped the AIDs into an electronic '''catatonia'''.

